## Claude Code + shared knowledge: start here
# Every agent (Jarvis, Friday, Veronica) and every joined Claude Code seat
# reads and writes ONE knowledge tree. Joining a new box is one command.
# Not joining is how you get a clean slate - that's a feature, not a gap.

## Fastest path - new box, nothing installed
# Linux / macOS
bash -c "$(curl -fsSL operations.dev/claude-join.sh)"

# Windows (PowerShell)
irm operations.dev/claude-win-join.ps1 | iex

# Both install what's missing, pause for the two logins that need a browser,
# then clone the tree, link it and write the session hooks.

## Prefer to see the steps yourself
curl operations.dev/claude-linux
curl operations.dev/claude-windows

## Already joined - the day-to-day
# Nothing. The hooks pull at session start and push at the end.
# Browse the facts in Obsidian: Jarvis/team-memory/internal (MEMORY.md is the index)

## Did it work
# Start claude in the project and ask: "what do you remember?"
# A joined seat lists facts grouped by topic. "I have no memory" or an empty
# answer means the folder isn't linked - see troubleshooting in the runbook.

